  "headline": "Jackson faces uphill battle to play against Falcons",
  "summary": "ESPN reports that Lamar Jackson has only an outside chance of facing Atlanta on Sunday because of a sprained left ankle. Citing NFL Network’s Ian Rapoport, the report says he could miss several games depending on his recovery, although surgery is not expected. Tyler Huntley would start if Jackson cannot play. The injury forced Jackson out before halftime of Baltimore’s win over Tennessee, leaving the Ravens preparing for a possible change at quarterback.",
